usage: live_play_v2.py [-h] [--card-choice {argmax,filtered}]
                       [--card-ratio CARD_RATIO] [--card-T CARD_T]
                       [--spell-aim {argmax,rocket_area}]
                       [--decision-seed DECISION_SEED] [--ckpt CKPT]
                       [--tau TAU] [--leak LEAK] [--no-anti-leak]
                       [--public-audit] [--interval-ms INTERVAL_MS]
                       [--max-seconds MAX_SECONDS] [--dry-run]
                       [--reader {v1,v2}] [--overlay {both,detector,reader}]
                       [--no-record] [--device {auto,cuda,cpu}]
                       [--extrapolate EXTRAPOLATE] [--no-opp-counter]
                       [--menu-guard] [--no-menu-guard]
                       [--invite-wait INVITE_WAIT] [--no-ability]
                       [--matches MATCHES] [--friend FRIEND] [--ladder]
                       [--wins-today WINS_TODAY] [--clip-every CLIP_EVERY]
                       [--stop-file STOP_FILE]
                       [--ckpt-override-file CKPT_OVERRIDE_FILE]
                       [--nav-dry-run]

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --card-choice {argmax,filtered}
  --card-ratio CARD_RATIO
  --card-T CARD_T
  --spell-aim {argmax,rocket_area}
                        rocket_area: maximise learned cell probability inside
                        the catalog Rocket radius
  --decision-seed DECISION_SEED
                        separate seeded card-choice stream; recorded with each
                        experiment
  --ckpt CKPT
  --tau TAU
  --leak LEAK           force a play at >= this elixir (unless --no-anti-leak)
  --no-anti-leak        honour the model's play/wait decision even at full
                        elixir; disable forced spending
  --public-audit        log public board/targets and model decisions,
                        including WAIT, independently of video
  --interval-ms INTERVAL_MS
  --max-seconds MAX_SECONDS
                        PER-MATCH wall-clock cap (reset each match): overtime
                        ends by 6,000 ticks = 300 s of game time, +
                        loading/countdown. Hitting it stops the whole run
  --dry-run             decide and log, never tap
  --reader {v1,v2}      memory reader: v2 (default since 2026-10-03: evolved
                        units, projectiles, effects) or v1
  --overlay {both,detector,reader}
                        replay style: detector = play.py-style YOLO boxes only
                        (cosmetic, e.g. for posts), reader = memory-reader
                        markers + taps, both
  --no-record           skip the overlaid replay (default: screenrecord +
                        reader boxes ->
                        icebow/data/overlayed_replays/live_<stamp>.mp4)
  --device {auto,cuda,cpu}
                        where the model runs; auto = cuda when available.
                        2026-09-26: on CPU with torch's default 16 threads,
                        other busy jobs pushed decisions from ~40 ms to
                        0.5-3.4 s
  --extrapolate EXTRAPOLATE
                        decide on the board this many ticks ahead, where the
                        card lands (~26 live; 0 = off). Screen (HANDOFF
                        L68as): +3.4 pp gen / +6.9 pp v6lat vs no
                        extrapolation at delay 26
  --no-opp-counter      feed the model opponent elixir = unknown instead of
                        the public-events counter
  --menu-guard          OPT-IN in-match menu guard: a screencap every <= 2 s
                        is classified; any menu stops the match and taps wait
                        for a fresh non-menu classification. Off by default:
                        its screencaps saturated adb live (2026-09-30). Needs
                        a 900x1600 screen
  --no-menu-guard       no-op, kept for compatibility (the menu guard is off
                        unless --menu-guard)
  --invite-wait INVITE_WAIT
                        friend loop: seconds to wait on the Social tab for the
                        friend's invite before sending ours (owner 2026-09-30:
                        20 s); a random 5-20 s re-delay is used only after
                        crossed invites
  --no-ability          never press the hero ability button (default: pressed
                        by hero_button.should_press when the deck holds a hero
                        and the button reads ready)
  --matches MATCHES     play this many matches back to back (default 1 = one
                        match, no navigation). > 1 needs --friend: between
                        matches friend_nav.py starts the next FRIENDLY 1v1
                        against that friend's bot; the previous match's
                        overlay renders in the background
  --friend FRIEND       the friend to play when --matches > 1; must be the
                        friend the nav templates were cropped for
  --ladder              with --matches > 1: re-queue Trophy Road matches via
                        ladder_nav.py (Play Again; after the day's 4th win OK
                        -> open the chests -> Battle) instead of friendlies
  --wins-today WINS_TODAY
                        ladder: set today's win count (daily chests come with
                        wins 1-4); default = ladder_state.json
  --clip-every CLIP_EVERY
                        seconds; > 0: record ONLY the first match and then one
                        match every this many seconds, and post a 60-s
                        overlaid clip of it to Discord (discord_clip.py) --
                        all other matches unrecorded
  --stop-file STOP_FILE
                        stop the run between matches once this file exists
  --ckpt-override-file CKPT_OVERRIDE_FILE
                        2026-10-03 deploy hook: if this file names a
                        checkpoint, it replaces --ckpt at start; if it changes
                        to a different checkpoint mid-run, the run exits
                        between matches so the supervisor restarts on it
  --nav-dry-run         play nothing: run ONE between-match navigation that
                        classifies the live screens and logs the tap it WOULD
                        make, never tapping (navigate by hand to test it)
